{
  "tema": 5102,
  "slug": "hay",
  "titulo": "Hay = there is / there are",
  "subtitulo": "«Hay olas. Hay una playa.»",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "Hay means both there is and there are: it never changes, whether one thing or many follows. It's the impersonal form of haber.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-17",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Hay** = _there is_ **and** _there are_. One form for everything."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "hay",
            "+",
            "un / una / number / mucho… / plural noun"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It's a special impersonal form of **haber**, so it never agrees with what follows."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Negative: **no hay**. Question: **¿Hay…?** (_Is there…? / Are there…?_)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Hay== una alberca en el hotel.",
              "en": "There's a pool at the hotel."
            },
            {
              "es": "Hoy ==hay== muchas olas en Playas.",
              "en": "There are lots of waves at Playas today."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Hay== tres tacos en el plato.",
              "en": "There are three tacos on the plate."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Hay== leche en el refri?",
              "en": "Is there milk in the fridge?"
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==hay== mucha gente en el gimnasio.",
              "en": "There aren't many people at the gym."
            },
            {
              "es": "En mi jardín ==hay== tomates y chiles.",
              "en": "There are tomatoes and chiles in my garden."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Están muchas olas hoy."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Hay muchas olas hoy."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "_There are_ = **hay**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Es una alberca aquí."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Hay una alberca aquí."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "_There is_ = **hay**, not **es**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Hay la playa cerca."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "La playa está cerca."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Not **hay el / la**: for a specific thing use **está**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "parientes",
      "titulo": "Related rules",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "hay vs está",
              "texto": "Which one when: [[7036|hay vs está]]."
            },
            {
              "forma": "hay un / una",
              "texto": "The articles after hay: [[5104|un, una]]."
            },
            {
              "forma": "he, has, ha… hay",
              "texto": "The verb behind it: [[5773|haber in the present]]."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "kwiz",
      "titulo": "Check yourself",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Say it out loud, then open the answer."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "mini_kwiz",
          "lista": [
            {
              "p": "In Spanish: _There are two dogs._",
              "r": "Hay dos perros.",
              "nota": "hay for plural too."
            },
            {
              "p": "In Spanish: _Is there coffee?_",
              "r": "¿Hay café?",
              "nota": "¿Hay…?"
            },
            {
              "p": "Fix it: _Son muchos carros aquí._",
              "r": "Hay muchos carros aquí.",
              "nota": "there are = hay."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
